{"number": 70, "text": "       32             Time         2:    clocks         and       frequency\n\n\n                      Clocks   / time  passing\n                      | If you...                                        | then you...                                 |\n                                                                       1                           hava limitad tima\n                       work  against the clock to get something done/finished work fast because you only have limited time\n                        do something in no time at all                     do it very quickly\n                             a day                                         decide to finish (usually finish working)\n                        don’t have a minute to call your own               are very busy indeed\n                        do something there and then (or then and there)    do it immediately, right at that moment\n                        get up / start at the crack of dawn                start very early in the morning\n\n                      Jake worked   against the clock to get the report finished before the meeting.\n                      The  homework  is very easy.     be able to do it in no time at all.\n                          really tired. Let’s call it a day now and come back to it next week.\n                       Ever since the twins were born, | haven’t had a minute to call my own.\n                       if a new idea is suggested, Allan is always keen to try it out there and then.\n                       As our plane was leaving at 8 a.m., we had to get up at the crack of dawn to be at the airport on time.\n\n |               B|    Frequency\n                             idiame rafar ta hau      (ar haw rarelv)          hannens.\n\n                        idiom                    | meaning                                   |\n                                                                                                RARELY\n                        once in a lifetime         never likely to happen again\n                        once in a blue moon        very rarely\n                        once and for all           finally and definitely\n                                                                                                MORE  FREQUENTLY\n                        off and on / on and off    sometimes, but not regularly or continuously\n                         from time to time         sometimes, but not regularly\n                         nine times out of ten     almost always                                FREQUENTLY\n\n\n                       Other   time   idioms\n                       if                            like clockwork. it happens exactly as planned and without problems.\n                       If you do something / start from scratch, you go right back to the beginning and start again.\n\n\n                          Wherever possible, put groups of idioms onto a scale, like the frequency scale in B above. You could\n                          use scales for idioms connected with size, feelings, difficulties, etc.\n\n\n                        English Idioms in Use Intermediate\n         68", "char_count": 3144, "mean_conf": 87.96, "word_count": 366, "words": [{"text": "68", "x0": 180, "y0": 3343, "x1": 221, "y1": 3371, "conf": 97, "bold": false}, {"text": "work", "x0": 473, "y0": 584, "x1": 566, "y1": 614, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "against", "x0": 577, "y0": 582, "x1": 709, "y1": 621, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "the", "x0": 720, "y0": 581, "x1": 780, "y1": 611, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "clock", "x0": 791, "y0": 579, "x1": 886, "y1": 611, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "to", "x0": 897, "y0": 583, "x1": 931, "y1": 610, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "get", "x0": 944, "y0": 581, "x1": 996, "y1": 618, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "something", "x0": 1008, "y0": 576, "x1": 1192, "y1": 615, "conf": 93, "bold": false},